---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Setting Up Git for Kernel Development | OGC Blog">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="post-meta">2026-04-15 — Kyle Gospodnetich</div>
    <h1>Setting Up Git for Kernel Development</h1>
    <p class="lead">How to configure git with gmail to send patches upstream using git send-email.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="markdown-shell">
      <article class="markdown-content">
        <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
        <p>You'll need <code>git</code> and <code>git-email</code> installed on your system. On most distros:</p>
        <pre><code># Arch
sudo pacman -S git

# Fedora
sudo dnf install git git-email

# Debian/Ubuntu
sudo apt install git git-email</code></pre>

        <h2>Configure git</h2>
        <p>Add the following to your <code>~/.gitconfig</code>:</p>
        <pre><code>[sendemail]
  smtpEncryption = tls
  smtpServer = smtp.gmail.com
  smtpUser = your.email@gmail.com
  smtpPort = 587
  smtppass = <app-password></code></pre>

        <h2>Generating an App Password</h2>
        <p>Gmail requires an app password, not your regular password. Visit your Google Account settings, navigate to <strong>Security</strong>, and under <strong>2-Step Verification</strong> find <strong>App passwords</strong>. Generate a new one labeled "Linux kernel patches".</p>

        <h2>Sending Your First Patch</h2>
        <p>Once configured, you can send patches with:</p>
        <pre><code>git send-email --to recipient@example.com --cc maintainer@example.com v1-0001-my-patch.patch</code></pre>
        <p>For kernel patches, the typical workflow is:</p>
        <pre><code>git format-patch -v2 --cover-letter -o /tmp/patches origin/main
git send-email --to linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org /tmp/patches/*.patch</code></pre>

        <h2>Useful Aliases</h2>
        <p>Add these to your shell RC for a smoother workflow:</p>
        <pre><code>alias ksend='git send-email --to linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org'
alias kprep='git format-patch -v2 --cover-letter -o /tmp/patches origin/main'</code></pre>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="back-link">
      <a href="/blog">← Back to Blog</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

